---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import "../styles/visitors.css";
---

<BaseLayout title="Visitors | Economic Machine Learning Lab">
    <section class="banner">
        <div class="banner-content">
            <h1>Visitors</h1>
            <p>Visits and exchanges with industry, government, and academic institutions</p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <div class="container visitors-layout">
        <main>
            <section class="visitors-intro">
                <h2>Visits to EML</h2>
                <p>EML welcomes visitors from industry, government, and academic institutions to exchange perspectives and discuss research collaborations. This page records upcoming and past visits.</p>
            </section>

            <section class="visitors-section" aria-labelledby="upcoming-visits">
                <h2 id="upcoming-visits">Upcoming Visits</h2>
                <article class="visitor-card">
                    <p class="visitor-date">November 13, 2026</p>
                    <h3><a href="https://www.kpx.or.kr/eng/">Korea Power Exchange (KPX)</a> — South Korea</h3>
                    <p class="visitor-names">Minwoo Jang and Yongsik Kim</p>
                    <p class="visitor-team">Supply and Demand Forecasting Team, Energy Planning Department</p>
                    <p>KPX operates South Korea's electricity market and power system and plays a central role in national electricity supply-and-demand planning.</p>
                </article>
            </section>

            <section class="visitors-section" aria-labelledby="visit-context">
                <h2 id="visit-context">Visit Background</h2>
                <article class="visitor-card">
                    <p>Representatives from Korea Power Exchange (KPX) will visit the EML Lab at Indiana University to discuss electricity demand forecasting, particularly the challenges of predicting large new electricity loads and managing long-term uncertainty. The visit was initiated by KPX to seek EML's perspectives on forecasting methodologies, data requirements, and ongoing research related to electricity demand forecasting.</p>
                    <p>EML Research Director Joon Y. Park, together with his research collaborators in Korea, including EML collaborator <a href="https://econ.cau.ac.kr/en/portfolio-items/choi-yongok/">Yongok Choi</a>, has been developing core electricity-demand forecasting models for KPX for more than 30 years. This longstanding relationship provides a strong foundation for continued research exchange and collaboration.</p>
                </article>
            </section>
        </main>
    </div>
</BaseLayout>
